Fields used for modelling (3 text, 7 non-text):
  field                 kind         why it is used
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  program               text         the applicant's own words for what they applied to; the strongest text signal
  university            text         institution selectivity differs enormously and the name encodes it
  term                  categorical  admissions cycles differ in competitiveness, so the cycle is a real covariate
  degree                categorical  Masters and PhD acceptance rates differ by more than 40 points
  us_or_international   categorical  domestic and international pools are evaluated against each other
  gpa                   numeric      the most widely reported academic scalar in the dataset
  gre                   numeric      quantitative score, sparse but highly informative where present
  gre_v                 numeric      verbal score, matters more for humanities programs
  gre_aw                numeric      analytical writing score, the weakest of the three but still reported
  comments              text         free text where applicants volunteer research, funding, and fit details

Available fields deliberately excluded from the model input:
  llm-generated-program     standardized duplicate of program; a fallback, never a second input
  llm-generated-university  standardized duplicate of university; fallback only, same reason
  raw_program               unnormalized concatenation of program and degree, both already used
  status                    this is the prediction target - including it would leak the label
  notification_date         only known after a decision arrives, so unavailable at prediction time
  date_added                posting date leaks the outcome timeline rather than the applicant profile
  url                       row identity only; used for deduplication, carries no admissions signal

Numeric dtypes after conversion:
  gpa       float64
  gre       float64
  gre_v     float64
  gre_aw    float64

